---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { ORGANIZATION } from "../lib/seo";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How 100k Studio GmbH handles personal data on 100k.studio."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="legal-page__draft">
    <p><strong>Draft — needs legal review.</strong> This is placeholder wording written to describe what the site appears to do. It has not been checked by a lawyer, and the third-party services listed below need confirming against what is actually running in production before this is published.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {ORGANIZATION.legalName}<br />
    {ORGANIZATION.address.street}, {ORGANIZATION.address.postalCode} {ORGANIZATION.address.city}, Germany<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${ORGANIZATION.email}`}>{ORGANIZATION.email}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    We are the controller for the personal data processed through this website, within the meaning of
    the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site is a portfolio. It sets no advertising cookies, runs no cross-site tracking, and does not
    build a profile of you. The only personal data we receive is what you send us yourself through the
    contact form or by email.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider records standard access data each time a page is requested: the requesting IP
    address, the time of the request, the page requested, the referring page, and the browser and
    operating system reported. This is technically necessary to deliver the site and to keep it secure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — our legitimate interest in operating a stable and secure website.
    Retention: [confirm the retention period with your hosting provider].
  </p>

  <h2>Contact form and email</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the contact form we process the name, email address and message you enter, in order to
    answer you. The submission is handled by our form provider, and the message reaches us by email.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where your enquiry concerns a possible contract, otherwise
    Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries. We keep enquiries for as long
    as needed to deal with them and to meet any statutory retention obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Processors and third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    [Confirm this list before publishing.] The following providers process data on our behalf or receive
    data as a necessary part of delivering this site:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting and delivery</strong> — serves the pages and records the access logs described above.</li>
    <li><strong>Media delivery (CDN and video streaming)</strong> — images and video are requested from a content delivery network, which receives your IP address as a technical requirement of delivering the file.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form provider</strong> — receives the contents of a submitted form in order to forward it to us.</li>
    <li><strong>Fonts</strong> — served from this domain, so no request is made to a third-party font provider.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where a provider processes data outside the EU or EEA, the transfer is covered by the appropriate
    safeguards under Art. 44 ff. GDPR. [Confirm which providers this applies to and on what basis.]
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies for analytics, advertising or tracking. [Confirm whether anything on the
    site stores data in the browser; if it does, describe it here and consider whether consent is
    required under § 25 TDDDG.]
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15)</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16)</li>
    <li>have your data erased (Art. 17)</li>
    <li>restrict how we process it (Art. 18)</li>
    <li>receive it in a portable format (Art. 20)</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21)</li>
    <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing carried out before withdrawal</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, write to <a href={`mailto:${ORGANIZATION.email}`}>{ORGANIZATION.email}</a>.
    You also have the right to complain to a supervisory authority — for us that is the Berlin
    Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We update this policy when the site or the services behind it change. This version is a draft and has
    not yet been reviewed.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
